#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:1
msgid "Release 2.36.0 (2026-11-16)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:3
msgid "Packaging"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:5
msgid ""
"Starting with this release, [`nix-installer`](https://github.com/NixOS/nix-"
"installer) binaries are shipped alongside other binary artifacts in "
"[releases.nixos.org](https://releases.nixos.org/?prefix=nix/nix-2.36.0/)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:7
msgid "You can run the installer with:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:9
msgid ""
"```\n"
"curl -sSfL https://channels.nixos.org/nix-latest/nix-installer | sh -s -- "
"install\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:13
msgid ""
"It's built for `x86_64-linux`, `aarch64-linux` and `aarch64-darwin` "
"platforms and only supports multi-user installations."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:15
msgid ""
"Cross-built binary releases for `powerpc64-linux` and `powerpc64le-linux` "
"platforms [\\#16274](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16274)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:17
msgid ""
"[Scripted installer](https://channels.nixos.org/nix-latest/install) supports "
"busybox-based systems (e.g. Alpine) in single-user mode [\\#16537](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16537)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:19
msgid ""
"The scripted installer sets the correct store mtime [\\#16558](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16558)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:21
msgid "Improvements"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:23
msgid ""
"Daemon worker spawning rework [\\#15857](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/"
"15857) [\\#16659](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16659)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:25
msgid ""
"Previously, `nix-daemon` accepting on the `nix-daemon.socket` would spawn a "
"worker process by `fork()`\\-ing without calling `execv*`. This has "
"historically been a source of issues around fork-unsafe dependencies and in "
"Nix itself. The most notorious instance of this issue has been Nix on macOS, "
"which discourages such use of fork(2), and has caused numerous issues in the "
"past (mostly around the use of `SecureTransport` TLS backend in libcurl and "
"aws-c-io)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:30
msgid ""
"Now `nix-daemon` spawns a worker processes by spawning and executing itself "
"in `--stdio` mode by redirecting stdin/stdout to the accepted socket and "
"forcing the trust level with the stabilised `--force-trusted` and `--force-"
"untrusted` flags. The path to the current binary is either `/proc/self/exe` "
"on Linux, acquired via `_NSGetExecutablePath` on macOS, or "
"`KERN_PROC_PATHNAME` sysctl on FreeBSD."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:34
msgid ""
"No functional changes are expected from this, though there are minor user-"
"visible behavioral changes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:36
msgid ""
"`nix-daemon` no longer needs to be restarted for `/etc/nix/nix.conf` changes "
"to take effect in the daemon _worker_ (note that this doesn't apply to "
"settings like `allowed-users` or `trusted-users`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:38
msgid ""
"The command line of the worker process no longer has the form `nix-daemon "
"<peer pid>`. Previously, the PID of the daemon client process was inserted "
"into `argv[1]`. This also obviates the need for passing the no-op `--daemon` "
"flag for making room for the PID in `argv[1]`. The peer PID is now part of "
"the `argv[0]` in the form of `nix-daemon.worker-<peer pid>`. This is an "
"internal debugging feature used for correlating the daemon _worker_ process "
"with its client."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:44
msgid ""
"`daemon-trust-override`, `--process-ops` stabilisation [\\#16637](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16637) [\\#16659](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/16659)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:47
msgid ""
"`daemon-trust-override` experimental feature has been stabilised. This "
"change was needed to facilitate the daemon worker spawning rework."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:50
msgid ""
"`--force-untrusted` now behaves correctly when the `--stdio` daemon worker's "
"store is another remote store backed by another daemon."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:52
msgid ""
"`--force-untrusted`, `--force-trusted`, `--default-trust`, `--process-ops` "
"flags accepted by `nix-daemon` and `nix daemon` are no longer experimental."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:54
msgid ""
"Daemon enables cgroup controllers for build cgroups [\\#9675](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/9675) [\\#16024](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/16024)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:56
msgid ""
"With `use-cgroups`, the daemon now enables the `cpu`, `memory`, `io` and "
"`pids` controllers in its cgroup's `cgroup.subtree_control`, so per-build "
"cgroups expose `memory.peak`, `io.stat` etc. instead of only `cpu.stat`. "
"This requires the controllers to be delegated to the daemon's cgroup (e.g. "
"systemd `Delegate=yes`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:62
msgid ""
"Nix now finds Darwin runtime garbage collector roots without `lsof` [\\#3011]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/3011) [\\#13990](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/13990)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:64
msgid ""
"On Darwin, the garbage collector now uses `libproc` to retain store paths "
"referenced by running processes through their working directories, open "
"files, mapped regions, or environment variables. This avoids the slow `lsof` "
"fallback and adds environment-variable roots, which `lsof` could not "
"discover."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:69
msgid ""
"macOS does not expose the environment variables of entitled binaries while "
"System Integrity Protection is enabled, so those roots remain unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:72
msgid ""
"`nix run`, `nix search` and `nix bundle` now auto-call functions [\\#5316]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/5316) [\\#15895](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15895)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:74
msgid ""
"If an [installable](../glossary.md#gloss-installable) given with `--file` or "
"`--expr` evaluates to a function, it is now called automatically, provided "
"each of its arguments has a default value or is passed with `--arg`/`--"
"argstr`. This makes `nix run`, `nix search` and `nix bundle` behave like "
"`nix build`, `nix shell`, `nix-build` and `nix-env --query`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:77
msgid ""
"For example, `nix run --impure --expr '{ pkgs ? import <nixpkgs> {} }: "
"pkgs.hello'` now works instead of failing with `error: attribute 'type' does "
"not exist`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:79
msgid ""
"`nix eval` and `nix edit`, which show the value itself rather than a "
"package, are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:81
msgid ""
"Build cgroups are named after the derivation [\\#16516](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/16516)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:83
msgid ""
"Per-build cgroups are now named `nix-build@<drv-hash>-<uid>` when a build "
"user is used, and `nix-build@<drv-hash>-<pid>` otherwise. They replace `nix-"
"build-uid-<uid>` and `nix-build-pid-<pid>-<counter>`, so external tools can "
"locate the cgroup of a given derivation's build."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:86
msgid ""
"Add an alias for optimise. [\\#1902](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/"
"1902) [\\#11326](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/11326) [\\#11577]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11577) [\\#15997](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15997)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:88
msgid ""
"Add \"optimize\" as a linguistic variation of \"optimise\". Now both the "
"`nix-store` and `nix store` commands work with the same spelling."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:90
msgid ""
"Downloads and store path copying produces significantly less log updates for "
"`internal-json` logger [\\#16671](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16671) "
"[\\#16670](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16670)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:92
msgid ""
"Tools such as `nix-output-monitor` were previously significantly "
"bottlenecked parsing on the order of tens of MB/s of JSON. Download progress "
"updates are now chunked and rate-limited. Bandwidth requirements for the "
"logger are now significantly lower."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:95
msgid ""
"Styled output on stdout is plain when stdout is not a terminal [\\#4626]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/4626) [\\#9486](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/9486) [\\#16710](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/16710) "
"[\\#16711](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16711)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:97
msgid ""
"`nix profile list`, `nix profile history`, `nix flake metadata`, `nix flake "
"show`, `nix search` and `nix store diff-closures` no longer write ANSI bold "
"and color to stdout when it is not a terminal, or when `NO_COLOR` is set. "
"Set `CLICOLOR_FORCE` to keep the styling."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:100
msgid ""
"Add `nix version` command with `--json` option [\\#16201](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/16201) A `--version` flag is more like a modern subcommand "
"than a flag, and this provides a place for JSON output, making it easier to "
"consume in scripts. When `--json` is passed, the output includes library "
"versions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:105
msgid ""
"`nix --version -vv` output also includes library versions in human-readable "
"comma-separated format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:107
msgid ""
"Bash completions now handle redirections [\\#16648](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/16648)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:109
msgid ""
"File names after redirections (e.g. `nix log nixpkgs#hello > /tmp/hello-"
"lo<TAB>`) can now be completed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:111
msgid ""
"Nix now makes use of reflinking via `copy_file_range` when copying files on "
"filesystem that support it [\\#15410](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"15410)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:113
msgid "Error message improvements"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:115
msgid ""
"Start of infinite recursion is now visible [\\#16296](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/16296)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:117
msgid ""
"When Nix reports a trace for an infinitely recursive evaluation, it will now "
"let you discern the cycle from the code that leads up to the cycle."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:120
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:122
msgid ""
"`nix eval --expr 'let f = builtins.add f 1; in toString f' --show-trace`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:140
msgid ""
"`builtins.warn` now supports unindented multi-line messages [\\#14794]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/14794)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:142
msgid ""
"`builtins.warn` now preserves the formatting of messages that start with a "
"newline instead of adding indentation to align them with the warning prefix."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:144
msgid ""
"`builtins.addErrorContext` keeps the error from _value_ when _context_ fails "
"[\\#8283](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/8283) [\\#16618](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16618)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:146
msgid ""
"If evaluating _context_ in [`builtins.addErrorContext context value`](../"
"language/builtins.md#builtins-addErrorContext) fails, the error from _value_ "
"now propagates, with the error from _context_ in its trace. Library authors "
"can therefore use more complex _context_ expressions without the risk of "
"hiding the error from _value_."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:149
msgid ""
"`addErrorContext` can no longer be abused to catch uncatchable errors like "
"`abort`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:151
msgid ""
"Error traces now show both the selection site in addition to the definition "
"site when an attribute is retrieved and both locations are known. [\\#16249]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16249)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:153
msgid ""
"Error traces now always show the derivations that were getting instantiated "
"[\\#16282](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16282)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:155
msgid ""
"All operators in error traces are displayed, and consistently [\\#16301]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16301)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:157
msgid ""
"Error messages for interrupted downloads are more concise [\\#16095](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16095) [\\#16646](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/16646) [\\#14757](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/14757)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:159
msgid "Bug fixes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:161
msgid ""
"`nix develop` no longer disables ASLR on Linux [\\#16624](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/16624)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:163
msgid ""
"Previously, `nix develop` would enable `ADDR_NO_RANDOMIZE` personality bit. "
"This disabled ASLR for all subsequent commands run in the devshell."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:166
msgid ""
"Additionally, `impersonate-linux-26` setting has been removed. If you "
"require this, you can change the personality manually or use `deterministic-"
"uname` from Nixpkgs depending on the use-case."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:169
msgid ""
"File descriptors are more reliably closed in children processes [\\#16247]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16247) [\\#16717](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/16717) [\\#16749](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16749)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:171
msgid ""
"Also, Nix daemon no longer performs 1 million close syscalls (commonly "
"configured RLIMIT_NOFILE for the daemon) for each spawned derivation builder "
"on macOS by relying on libproc for closing file descriptors in the child."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:174
msgid ""
"`post-build-hook` is no longer run in a mount namespace with a writable Nix "
"store [\\#16247](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16247)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:176
msgid ""
"`builtins.pathExists` no longer swallows access errors from evaluating its "
"argument [\\#16728](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16728)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:178
msgid ""
"Since Nix 2.20, `builtins.pathExists` accidentally recovered from access "
"errors caused by evaluating its argument. Consider:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:181
msgid "'builtins.pathExists (builtins.readFile /etc/passwd)'"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:184
msgid ""
"This evaluated to `false`, even though `builtins.readFile /etc/passwd` would "
"throw, and `builtins.pathExists` never saw a supposed path."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:186
msgid ""
"Now the error propagates, as it did in Nix 2.19 and earlier. This invocation "
"fails with the same error observed by calling `builtins.readFile /etc/"
"passwd` in isolation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:188
msgid ""
"Store garbage collector can now delete App bundles on macOS [\\#16626]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16626) [\\#16719](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/16719)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:190
msgid ""
"Previously, even when run as `root` Nix attempted to make directories "
"writable for deletion, which is not allowed for App bundles on macOS and "
"would fail with `Operation not permitted`. Nix now skips the `chmod` when "
"run as root on macOS."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:194
msgid ""
"Additionally, when run with `DAC_OVERRIDE` capability on Linux, `chmod` "
"operation is also skipped."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:196
msgid ""
"`nix eval --write-to` is stricter about what it writes [\\#16760](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16760)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:198
msgid ""
"`nix eval --write-to` now requires attributes to correspond to a single file "
"name. In particular, it rejects attribute names that contain `/` or are "
"empty, in addition to rejecting `.` and `..` as it did already. Previously, "
"an attribute such as `{ \"a/b\" = \"...\"; }` was written to a nested path "
"`a/b`, which is a bit of an \"injection\"."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:202
msgid ""
"Attribute sets can also now be nested at most 64 levels deep, the same limit "
"as for NARs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:204
msgid ""
"(The output is also now written in the same way as NARs are unpacked, which "
"hardens it in a bunch of ways.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:206
msgid "Path-like flake references detect Mercurial checkouts"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:208
msgid ""
"A path-like flake reference such as `.` used to become a `git+file:` input "
"only inside a Git repository, and a `path:` input everywhere else. In a "
"Mercurial checkout that copied the whole directory to the store, `.hg` and "
"untracked files included, and the flake had no `rev`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:211
msgid ""
"Such a reference now resolves to `hg+file:`, so only tracked files are "
"copied. This needs the `hg` executable, as `hg+file:` inputs always did."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:214
msgid ""
"Input schemes, including ones from [`plugin-files`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-plugin-files), can resolve a path-like flake reference to their "
"own scheme by implementing `InputScheme::localRepoURL()`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:216
msgid "S3: `endpoint=host:port` fixed, deprecated in favour of full URLs"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:218
msgid ""
"Bare `host:port` values for the `endpoint` parameter of `s3://` store URLs "
"were misparsed (the host was taken as a URL scheme). This is fixed, but the "
"bare form and the separate `scheme` parameter are deprecated: use a full URL "
"such as `endpoint=https://minio.example.com` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:223
msgid ""
"Boost.Context bug causing incorrect daemeon exception detection has been "
"worked around in Nix and Nixpkgs, with a fix contributed upstream [\\#16197]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16197) [\\#16174](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/16174)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:225
msgid ""
"This would cause spurious aborts in `nix repl` when `builtins.toFile` or "
"other primops that fetch to the store failed. It only affected builds of Nix "
"using Boost's fcontext coroutine backend with libstdc++ standard library."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:228
msgid ""
"NUL bytes in derivation `builder` and `args` attributes are rejected "
"[\\#16245](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16245)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:230
msgid ""
"This issue was not possible to encounter from the Nix evaluator, since Nix "
"strings disallow embedded NUL bytes but could lead to silent truncation in "
"other cases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:233
msgid ""
"Derivation parser is now more strict [\\#16237](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/16237) [\\#16284](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16284)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:235
msgid ""
"The derivation ATerm parser now rejects derivations that are not in the form "
"that's produced by the evaluator."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:237
msgid ""
"The NAR parser is stricter when file contents are discarded [\\#16325]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16325)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:239
msgid ""
"When computing the NAR listing (`.ls` files) and other operations that "
"discard contents of regular files in NARs, Nix did not sufficiently validate "
"padding bytes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:242
msgid ""
"Store path basenames that don't have the hash part followed by `-` are "
"properly rejected [\\#16257](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16257)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:244
msgid ""
"Truncated Brotli compressed NARs no longer cause Nix to loop infinitely "
"[\\#16575](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16575)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:246
msgid ""
"Errors while writing to compressed streams (e.g. copying to a local binary "
"cache store) no longer cause a crash [\\#16664](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/16664)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:248
msgid ""
"Non-lexically-canonical home-path literals (e.g. `~/repos/nixpkgs/.`) no "
"longer crash the evaluator [\\#16651](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"16651)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:250
msgid ""
"Deleting profiles with unexpected `mtime` no longer triggers a crash "
"[\\#16634](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16634)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:252
msgid ""
"Internal source tree names no longer leak into evaluation results of "
"`builtins.toXML` and value printing [\\#16780](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/16780)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:254
msgid ""
"This is a regression from 2.32 for `pure-eval` mode, which is now fixed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:256
msgid ""
"`builtins.readDir builtins.storeDir` no longer fails in impure evaluation "
"mode [\\#16780](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16780)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:258
msgid ""
"Since 2.32, it would fail with `error: path '/nix/store/' is not in the Nix "
"store`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:260
msgid ""
"Logging has been hardened against crafted inputs [\\#16784](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16784) [\\#16456](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/16456)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:262
msgid ""
"Nix now handles malformed inputs from derivation builders more robustly and "
"warns on unknown activities and result types."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:264
msgid ""
"While reading git objects, Nix now rejects duplicate Git tree entries and "
"unsorted trees [\\#16793](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16793)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:266
msgid "`ca-derivations`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:268
msgid ""
"Add new `nix store build-trace delete` command [\\#15655](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15655)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:270
msgid ""
"Implement new `builder-rpc-v0` feature; see [\\#15793](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/15793) below under `dynamic-derivations`. While motivated "
"primarily by the dynamic derivations feature, registering outputs is also "
"useful for content-addressing derivations. The builder can learn the "
"calculated content-addressed path of one of its outputs before creating "
"others, removing the need for any rewriting on the nix-daemon side after the "
"derivation finishes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:274
msgid ""
"Error instead of crashing when realisations cannot be queried [\\#16014]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16014)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:276
msgid "`dynamic-derivations`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:278
msgid ""
"Implement new `builder-rpc-v0` feature [\\#15793](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/15793) This PR adds support for creating new store objects within a "
"derivation at runtime, then registering them as an output."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:281
msgid ""
"`nix store add --scan` for creating references, as well as in `builder-rpc-"
"v0` [\\#16163](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/16163)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:283
msgid "C API"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.36.md:285
msgid ""
"Expose evaluator helpers for working with derivation trees [\\#15842]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/15842) `nix_get_derivation`, "
"`nix_value_auto_call_function`"
msgstr ""

